==English==

===Alternative forms===
*{{alter|en|pacificist|q1=dated}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|pacifiste}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpæsɪfɪst/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pacifist.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who loves, supports, or favours [[peace]].
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Mahatma Gandhi}} was one of the world's most famous '''pacifists'''.}}
## One who prefers to avoid [[violence]] in daily life.
## One who is [[anti-war]].
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=[[w: Chris Wallace (journalist)|Chris Wallace]]|title=Character: Profiles in Presidential Courage
|passage=No matter what '''pacifist''' "flubdubs and flapdoodle mollycoddles" might say, the President [Teddy Roosevelt] knew that if there were a general war then America could well be drawn into it.}}
##One who both abstains from inflicting violence on others and opposes others doing so.
# {{lb|en|video games|[[roguelike]]s}} A [[player]] who attempts the [[challenge]] of winning a game without [[attack]]ing any enemy characters.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or relating to [[pacifism]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Charles R. Pinches|author2=Kelly S. Johnson|author3=Charles M. Collier|title=Unsettling Arguments: A Festschrift on the Occasion of Stanley Hauerwas's 70th Birthday|publisher=Wipf and Stock Publishers|isbn=9781606082539|page=129
|passage=Therefore, because Hauerwas is a United Methodist, a church that is clearly not '''pacifist''' even if it is not clear what it is, he is not (yet) a pacifist.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|one who loves, supports, or favours peace}} {{l|en|dove}}, {{l|en|Gandhist}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|one who loves, supports, or favours peace}} {{l|en|bellicist}}, {{l|en|militarist}}, {{l|en|hawk}}

====Derived terms====
* [[anarcho-pacifist]]

====Related terms====
